:71,"section":"A","questionNumber":"16","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Table 4 shows the index of consumer prices and the unemployment rate for an economy. The data is for the end of each quarter in a particular year. The index of consumer prices for the final quarter of the previous year was 120.9. According to the data, it can be concluded that","topics":["2-3-3-inflation-and-deflation","2-3-2-employment-and-unemployment","2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["inflation","unemployment","price index"],"qpPage":15,"msPage":3,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["prices were lower at the start of the year and employment was lower at the end of the year.","the quarterly inflation rate fluctuated whilst the unemployment rate increased throughout the year.","the relationship between the change in the inflation and unemployment rates was positive in each quarter.","there was an inverse relationship between prices and unemployment in each quarter."],"usesFigure":true},{"id":"aqa-p3-2024-jun-q16","p":70,"section":"A","questionNumber":"16","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"An economy's long-run trend rate of economic growth in real gross domestic product (GDP) is 2.8% per annum. In 2018, the economy's actual real GDP was equal to its trend level of real GDP. Table 4 shows the economy's actual rate of growth in real GDP over a five-year period. All other things being equal, in which year was the economy likely to experience the most inflationary pressure?","topics":["2-3-1-economic-growth-and-the-economic-cycle","2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["output gap","inflationary pressure","trend growth"],"qpPage":11,"msPage":3,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["2020","2021","2022","2023"],"usesFigure":true},{"id":"aqa-p2-2023-jun-q12","p":60,"section":"B","questionNumber":"12","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":25,"questionText":"Evaluate how, in the long-run, governments could try to reconcile conflicts between the various objectives of economic policy.","topics":["2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["policy conflicts","macroeconomic objectives","long run"],"qpPage":6,"msPage":19,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p3-2023-jun-q16","p":69,"section":"A","questionNumber":"16","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Figure 4 shows a short-run Phillips curve (SRPC) and a long-run Phillips curve (LRPC). Government intervention moves the economy from position A to position B and then the economy moves from position B to position C. Which one of the following is most likely to explain the movement from position B to position C?","topics":["2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives","2-3-3-inflation-and-deflation"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["Phillips curve","inflation expectations","natural rate of unemployment"],"qpPage":17,"msPage":3,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["Demand for exports has risen as a result of the intervention","Economic agents have higher inflation expectations due to the intervention","The government cut taxes to reduce unemployment","The intervention has increased the natural rate of unemployment"],"usesFigure":true},{"id":"aqa-p2-2022-jun-q6","p":59,"section":"A","questionNumber":"6","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"Explain how the data in Extract D (Figures 3 and 4) show that there may be a short-run trade-off between unemployment and inflation.","topics":["2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["Phillips curve","unemployment","inflation","trade-off"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":13,"ctxPage":4,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p3-2021-jun-q4","p":67,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Which one of the following changes in macroeconomic performance is most likely to involve a trade-off, at least in the short-run, between the objectives of government macroeconomic policy?","topics":["2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives","2-1-1-the-objectives-of-government-economic-policy"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["policy conflicts","trade-off","macroeconomic objectives"],"qpPage":4,"msPage":3,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["Economic growth increases and the deficit on the balance of payments on current account is eliminated","Inflation declines to match its target rate and the government’s budget position moves into balance","The distribution of income becomes more equal as economic growth increases","The government’s budget deficit increases as the rate of unemployment is reduced"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"aqa-p2-2020-jun-q12","p":57,"section":"B","questionNumber":"12","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":25,"questionText":"Evaluate the view that the main objectives of UK government macroeconomic policy can be achieved without conflicting with each other.","topics":["2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["policy conflicts","macroeconomic objectives","trade-offs"],"qpPage":6,"msPage":19,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p3-2020-jun-q19","p":66,"section":"A","questionNumber":"19","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"The long-run Phillips curve shows that","topics":["2-3-4-possible-conflicts-between-macroeconomic-policy-objectives"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["long-run Phillips curve","natural rate of un